WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:02.499
And now, great moments in unintended

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.509
consequences.

00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:05.510
Part one: See Shores.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:06.920
The year: 2003.

00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:09.339
The problem: There's a photo of

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:10.989
Barbra Streisand's house on the

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:11.919
Internet.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.049
The solution: sue the photographer

00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:15.909
for $50 million

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:18.219
and demand the photo be removed.

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:20.079
Sounds like a great idea, with

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:21.339
the best of intentions.

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:23.379
What could possibly go wrong?

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:25.089
It turns out when you try and hide

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:27.069
something, people get interested.

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:28.779
The aerial image, part of a larger

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:30.909
project to document coastal erosion,

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:33.129
had only been downloaded six times

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:34.989
before Streisand got upset.

00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:36.339
But in the month following the

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:38.649
lawsuit, over 400,000

00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:40.089
people clicked on the image of

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:41.379
Streisand's house.

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:43.239
Babs lost her case, was forced to

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:45.129
pay 177,000 in

00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:47.139
legal fees and the Streisand

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:49.209
effect is now shorthand for bringing

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:51.279
unwanted attention to the very thing

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:52.719
being suppressed.

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:54.699
Maybe next time, don't mention

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:56.799
it. Part two: Open

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:58.209
Sesame.

00:00:58.210 --> 00:00:59.589
The year: 2022.

00:00:59.590 --> 00:01:01.419
The problem: Over

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:03.249
a million Americans are allergic

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:04.869
to sesame seeds.

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:06.789
The solution: Add them to

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:09.279
the FDA's major allergens list,

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:10.929
which requires food manufacturers

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:12.279
and restaurants to disclose if

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:13.809
products either contain or might

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:16.299
have come in contact with the seeds.

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:18.129
Sounds like a great idea, with

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:19.389
the best of intentions.

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:21.639
What could possibly go wrong?

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:23.769
Turns out sesame seeds are small

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:25.749
and a bit hard to keep track of,

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:27.429
making it frustrating and expensive

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:29.409
to guarantee seeds will not cross

00:01:29.410 --> 00:01:30.999
contaminate other foods.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.949
Under the stringent FDA rules, it's

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:34.629
not good enough to simply state that

00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:36.909
a food may contain or is produced

00:01:36.910 --> 00:01:39.189
in a facility that uses sesame.

00:01:39.190 --> 00:01:40.749
So rather than go through the cost

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:42.189
and hassle of assuring there are

00:01:42.190 --> 00:01:43.659
none in their product, companies

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:45.549
simply added small amounts and

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:46.929
included it to the list of

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:47.739
ingredients.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:48.549
Presto.

00:01:48.550 --> 00:01:50.079
Problem solved.

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:52.479
Unless, you know, you're allergic.

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:55.269
Part three: Oddball.

00:01:55.270 --> 00:01:57.219
The year: 1994.

00:01:57.220 --> 00:01:59.229
The problem: Ties in soccer

00:01:59.230 --> 00:02:00.429
on boring.

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:02.289
The solution: Organizers

00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:04.359
of the Caribbean Cup made game

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:06.399
winning overtime goals count

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:08.228
double, pushing teams to

00:02:08.229 --> 00:02:11.019
play aggressively in extra time.

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:12.879
Sounds like a great idea, with

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:14.169
the best of intentions.

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:16.449
What could possibly go wrong?

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:17.450
It turns out...math.

00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:20.589
In the last group game of the

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:22.449
tournament, Barbados needed to beat

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:24.369
Grenada by two goals to reach

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:25.269
the final.

00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:27.639
Otherwise, Grenada would advance.

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:29.349
With only minutes left in the match,

00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:31.179
Barbados found themselves up by

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:33.219
only a single goal.

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:34.749
Realizing their predicament,

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:37.749
Barbados scored on themselves.

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:39.249
So long as they could keep the game

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:40.309
tied during regular play, Barbados

00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:43.239
could win by two with a single

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:44.859
score in overtime.

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:46.329
What followed was one of the most

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:48.339
bizarre 5 minutes in the history

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:50.409
of the game, with Barbados defending

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:52.509
both goals, while Grenada tried

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:54.339
to score in either end of the

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:55.149
field.

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:57.189
Grenada failed, Barbados scored

00:02:57.190 --> 00:02:59.079
in overtime and the rule was

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:00.699
dropped. And then it rolled around

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:01.899
on the pitch for a while, grabbing

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:03.459
its knees, screaming for a penalty.

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:04.559
Oh, I'm so hurt.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:05.560
Go....re-evaluate

00:03:07.990 --> 00:03:08.990
your priors.

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:11.049
Great moments and unintended

00:03:11.050 --> 00:03:12.189
consequences.

00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:14.619
Good intentions, bad results.

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:15.879
Do you have an idea for a future

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:17.619
episode? Put it in the comments.

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:18.819
I'd like to read.

